[32m+[m[32m## Security design[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m- **Passwords**: bcrypt (cost 12); policy of 10+ chars with upper/lower/number/symbol, no username or common passwords. Hashes never leave the server.[m
[32m+[m[32m- **Admin accounts cannot be registered.** The sign-up endpoint rejects `role: admin` (and logs it). The admin API cannot create admins either; only `npm run seed:admin` can.[m
[32m+[m[32m- **Sessions**: signed JWT in an **HttpOnly, SameSite=Strict** cookie (`Secure` in production). No token is ever readable by page JavaScript or stored in `localStorage`.[m
[32m+[m[32m- **Instant revocation**: every user has a `token_version`. Changing a password, an admin reset, or a suspension invalidates all existing sessions immediately.[m
[32m+[m[32m- **Brute-force defence**: failed sign-ins are rate limited per IP, and an account locks for 15 minutes after 5 wrong passwords. Unknown usernames take the same time as wrong passwords, and error messages are generic.[m
[32m+[m[32m- **CSRF**: SameSite cookies plus a required `X-Requested-With` header and an `Origin` check on every write; JSON-only bodies.[m
[32m+[m[32m- **Authorisation on the server**: every route checks the role, and shopkeepers are checked against `shop_owners` for every shop or offer they touch.[m
[32m+[m[32m- **Headers**: Helmet with a strict Content-Security-Policy (no inline scripts), `frame-ancestors 'none'`, HSTS in production.[m
[32m+[m[32m- **Input safety**: parameterised SQL everywhere, validated fields, images limited to PNG/JPEG/WEBP/GIF under 1.5 MB (SVG is refused), website links must be `http(s)`, all dashboard output is HTML-escaped.[m
[32m+[m[32m- **Only `public/` is served.** Previously the whole project folder was exposed, including `.env`. That is fixed and covered by tests.[m
[32m+[m[32m- **Errors**: details go to the server log; browsers only see a generic message. CORS `*` was removed.[m
[32m+[m[32m- **Audit trail**: sign-ins, failures, lockouts, admin actions and edits are stored in `mall.audit_log` and shown in the admin *Security log*.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m### Before going live[m
[32m+[m[32m- Set `NODE_ENV=production` and serve over **HTTPS** (nginx, Caddy or your host). This enables `Secure` cookies and HSTS.[m
[32m+[m[32m- Set `TRUST_PROXY=1` when behind one reverse proxy so rate limits see real client IPs.[m
[32m+[m[32m- Use a strong, unique `DB_PASSWORD` and a dedicated DB user with only the rights the app needs, not the `postgres` superuser.[m
[32m+[m[32m- Back up the database regularly (see below).[m
